<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Continuum Modeling — Biological Transport Networks</title>

  <!-- Keep site theme to match index -->
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/ccb.css" />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

  <style>
    :root { --maxw: 1000px; --card: #fff; }
    body { font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; color:#0e0e0e; }
    .wrap { max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.6rem 1rem 2rem; }

    /* Sticky header (matches index) */
    header.site {
      position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1000;
      padding: 1rem 0;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.85);
      backdrop-filter: saturate(180%) blur(8px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.07);
    }
    .topnav a { margin-right: 1rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; padding:.4rem .1rem; }
    .topnav a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    /* HERO */
    .hero { max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 1rem auto 0; padding: 0 1rem; position: relative; }
    .hero-media { height: clamp(280px, 42vw, 420px); border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden; position: relative; background:#000; }
    .hero-media video, .hero-media img, .hero-media iframe, .hero-media object { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; object-fit: cover; }
    .hero--overlay::after {
      content: ""; position: absolute; left: 1rem; right: 1rem; bottom: 0; height: 55%;
      border-bottom-left-radius: 12px; border-bottom-right-radius: 12px;
      background: linear-gradient(0deg, rgba(0,0,0,.65), rgba(0,0,0,0));
      pointer-events: none;
    }
    .hero-title {
      position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: center;
      padding: 0 2rem 1.25rem; text-align: center;
    }
    .hero-title .inner {
      display:inline-block; padding: .45rem .9rem; border-radius: 10px;
      background: rgba(0,0,0,.35); backdrop-filter: blur(2px) saturate(120%);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.25);
    }
    .hero-title h1 {
      color: #fff; margin: 0; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .01em;
      font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.6vw, 2.6rem);
      text-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.5), 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.45), 0 6px 22px rgba(0,0,0,.6);
    }
    .hero-title .subhead { color: rgba(255,255,255,.96); margin-top: .25rem; font-weight: 600; }

    /* Breadcrumbs */
    .crumbs { font-weight: 600; margin: .6rem 0 1.1rem; padding: 0 1rem; }
    .crumbs a { text-decoration: none; }
    .crumbs a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    /* Page-like sections */
    .page { background: var(--card); border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 2px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.06); padding: 1.1rem; margin: 1.4rem 0; }
    .page h2 { margin: .2rem 0 1rem; font-size: 1.35rem; }
    .two-col { display:grid; grid-template-columns: 1.25fr 0.95fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start; }
    .card { background:#fff; border-radius:12px; padding:1rem 1.1rem; box-shadow:0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.06); }
    .card p { margin: .45rem 0; }

    /* Figures & captions */
    figure { margin: 0; }
    .media { border-radius:12px; overflow:hidden; background:#000; }
    .media img, .media video { width:100%; height:auto; display:block; }
    figcaption { font-size:.92rem; opacity:.78; margin-top:.5rem; }
    .full { grid-column: 1 / -1; }

    /* Pills / quick links */
    .pill {
      display:inline-block; font-size:.85rem; font-weight:600; text-decoration:none;
      padding:.28rem .7rem; border:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.12); border-radius:999px; margin:.25rem .35rem .25rem 0;
      background:#f7f7f7;
    }
    .pill:hover { background:#fff; }

    @media (max-width: 880px){
      .two-col { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <!-- Header -->
  <header class="site">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div style="font-size:1rem; font-weight:800;">Biological Transport Networks</div>
      <div style="opacity:.8;">Center for Computational Biology · Flatiron Institute</div>
      <nav class="topnav" style="margin-top:.5rem;">
        <a href="index.html#mission">Mission</a>
        <a href="index.html#research">Research</a>
        <a href="index.html#people">People</a>
        <a href="index.html#publications">Publications</a>
        <a href="index.html#news">News</a>
        <a href="index.html#contact">Contact</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- HERO: video banner -->
  <section class="hero hero--overlay">
    <div class="hero-media">
      <video src="images/videos/random_sphere.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline></video>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-title">
      <div class="inner">
        <h1>Network Homogenization</h1>
        <div class="subhead">Discrete-to-continuum modeling of biological transport networks</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
  <div class="crumbs wrap"><a href="index.html#research">← Back to Research</a></div>

  <!-- PAGE 1: intro with spiderweb + text, then graphs under it -->
  <main class="wrap">
    <section class="page">
      <div class="two-col">
        <figure>
          <div class="media">
            <img src="images/spiderweb.png" alt="Complex network pattern resembling spiderweb" />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            Representative network geometry. We analyze transport on graphs and relate it to continuum limits.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <aside class="card">
          <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Summary</h2>
          <p>
            We present a homogenization framework that maps discrete network transport to an effective continuum description,
            capturing macroscopic flow, anisotropy, and adaptation laws while accounting for microstructural variability.
          </p>
          <p>
            The approach links graph Laplacians and constitutive relations to PDEs with effective coefficients, enabling
            fast simulation, parameter inference, and comparison against high-resolution network dynamics.
          </p>
          <div style="margin-top:.8rem;">
            <strong>Quick links:</strong><br/>
            <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2301.07086" class="pill">Preprint</a>
            <!-- Add more as needed -->
          </div>
        </aside>

        <!-- “Different graphs” figure full width below -->
        <figure class="full" style="margin-top:.8rem;">
          <div class="media">
            <img src="images/different_graphs.png" alt="Network ensembles and statistics" />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            Ensembles of graphs used for averaging: varying connectivity, degree distributions, and spatial embedding.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PAGE 2: discrete vs continuum comparison -->
    <section class="page">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Discrete vs. Continuum Adaptation</h2>
      <figure>
        <div class="media">
          <img src="images/discrete_vs_continuum_adaptation.png" alt="Side-by-side comparison of discrete network adaptation and continuum model" />
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          Quantitative comparison of adaptation dynamics: the continuum model reproduces key statistics of the discrete network evolution.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <!-- Bottom animation/video -->
      <figure style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        <div class="media" style="background:#000;">
          <video src="images/run0_C_animation.mp4" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls></video>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          Time-lapse of continuum concentration field corresponding to a discrete network adaptation experiment.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <div class="wrap" style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <div>&copy; <span id="year"></span> Biological Transport Networks · Flatiron Institute</div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('year').textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
